{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "03NV", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\`e", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-fpqc}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:26bd7c97dbd4f3e7a0e52db4eebe1417cb1e0358fb6e42bb5319055a40aa4680", "source_text": "The first condition corresponds to fp, which stands for\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>fid<ACCENT_0001>lement plat<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>, faithfully flat in french, and\nthe second to qc, <TEXTITOPEN_0002>quasi-compact<TEXTITCLOSE_0002>. The second part of\nthe first condition is unnecessary when the second condition holds.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d95ed560ad612f1060d1360b7d41db37edc8445837ca269649c8e2f652826ebe", "unit_id": "tag:03NX:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "example", "parent_tag": "03NV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{\\Spec(B) \\to \\Spec(A)\\}$", "MATH_0003": "$A \\to B$", "MATH_0004": "$f: X \\to Y$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{ f: X\\to\nY\\}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\varphi :\n\\coprod_{x \\in \\mathbf{A}^1_k} \\Spec(\\mathcal{O}_{\\mathbf{A}^1_k, x})\n\\to \\mathbf{A}^1_k$", "MATH_0007": "$k$", "MATH_0008": "$\\{\\varphi\\}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathbf{A}^2_k = \\Spec(k[x, y])$", "MATH_0010": "$i_x : D(x) \\to \\mathbf{A}^2_k$", "MATH_0011": "$i_y : D(y) \\to \\mathbf{A}^2_k$", "MATH_0012": "$\\{i_x, i_y, \\Spec(k[[x, y]]) \\to \\mathbf{A}^2_k\\}$", "MATH_0013": "$\\{i_x, i_y, \\Spec(\\mathcal{O}_{\\mathbf{A}^2_k, 0}) \\to \\mathbf{A}^2_k\\}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\item", "STRUCT_0007": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{example}\n\\label{example-fpqc-coverings}\n", "suffix": "\\end{example}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f7bd1becf7aed5a46d8c92d2b80c8c0d3e19c3de0609f2dd24392ba1390f4db4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1fcf33954a856c167cea27d7c518e2d2c7518eaec88bb2a767b9789c97e17bd0", "source_text": "Examples of fpqc coverings.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> Any Zariski open covering of <MATH_0001> is an fpqc covering.\n<STRUCT_0003> A family <MATH_0002> is an fpqc\ncovering if and only if <MATH_0003> is a faithfully flat ring map.\n<STRUCT_0004> If <MATH_0004> is flat, surjective and quasi-compact, then <MATH_0005> is an fpqc covering.\n<STRUCT_0005> The morphism\n<MATH_0006>,\nwhere <MATH_0007> is a field, is flat and surjective. It is not quasi-compact, and\nin fact the family <MATH_0008> is not an fpqc covering.\n<STRUCT_0006> Write\n<MATH_0009>. Denote <MATH_0010>\nand <MATH_0011> the standard opens.\nThen the families\n<MATH_0012>\nand\n<MATH_0013>\nare fpqc coverings.\n<STRUCT_0007>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c4c2663890c04b5c2b9d4764bb368c1adb2e89b918b7cd9d1aabb9c4611f0f5e", "unit_id": "tag:03NY:statement"}
